<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="UTF-8"/><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"/><title>Inside Agent House</title></head><body><main class="ah-about"><a href="/">Return to the house</a><p>THE IDEA</p><h1>A memory should leave a trace.<br/>And a trace should have a reason.</h1><p>Agent House turns a fictional agent's personality and reviewed memories into an isometric room. This is an interface to structured content, not a claim that an AI has a private inner life.</p><h2>Try the correction.</h2><ol><li>Choose the empty chair and read quietly.</li><li>Inspect the proposed memory. One quiet visit should not dictate every future visit.</li><li>Change the scope to evening reading visits and keep it.</li><li>Switch to morning. The unapproved generalization should not follow you there.</li><li>Click the remembered object to trace the encounter, proposal and human correction.</li></ol><h2>Personality becomes affordance.</h2><p>Privacy changes where a visitor sits. Sociability changes a greeting. Warmth changes where tea belongs. Curiosity makes room for books. Explicit boundaries protect particular activities. These rules are inspectable and deterministic.</p><h2>Two honest modes.</h2><p>The visitor demo uses authored character responses and changes only this browser tab. It does not call AI or write to Sanity. The authenticated owner studio uses Sanity Agent Prompt for bounded responses and proposals. The model cannot directly approve memories or change the published house.</p><h2>The content graph.</h2><p>Agent profiles, meaningful objects, observed interactions, proposed meanings, approved memories and published house snapshots are distinct document types. Evidence references connect them. Approval is revision-checked and transactional; archiving removes a memory's influence while preserving its trace.</p><h2>What is and is not verified.</h2><p>This is an in-progress competition build. Live AI, persistence and cross-tab verification must pass before submission. No acceptance, prize or revenue is claimed. All resident profiles and events in this public dataset are fictional; never enter private information.</p><p>Built with Astro, Sanity Studio, App SDK and Agent Actions. Code and artwork are AI-generated and explicitly tested. The development account will distinguish actual results from plans.</p><p><a href="https://dev.to/challenges/sanity-2026-09-16">DEV Sanity Challenge</a> · <a href="https://www.sanity.io/docs/app-sdk/sdk-authentication">Authentication model</a> · <a href="https://www.sanity.io/docs/content-lake/transactions">Transaction semantics</a></p></main></body></html>
